    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327932/comment/12363499",
          "id": "12363499",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "two things i forgot to mention before...\n\n1) It seems i can as many 4mb documents as my heart desires, but once i go up to 5 all hell breaks loose.\n\n2) I didn't try playing with the various IndexWriter options to see what affect they had on the breaking point.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "created": "2006-01-21T11:37:33.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-01-21T11:37:33.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327932/comment/12363524",
          "id": "12363524",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=lucenebugs%40danielnaber.de",
            "name": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "key": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Daniel Naber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "writer.setMaxBufferedDocs(5); solves to OOM error, at least for binary stuff that's 5MB. So with writer.setMaxBufferedDocs(1) you can probably add documents that are almost as big as your JVM maximum memory I guess.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=lucenebugs%40danielnaber.de",
            "name": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "key": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Daniel Naber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-01-22T05:15:47.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-01-22T05:15:47.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327932/comment/12363568",
          "id": "12363568",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=lucenebugs%40danielnaber.de",
            "name": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "key": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Daniel Naber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "writer.setMaxBufferedDocs(1) was a bad idea, it doesn't work because of an off-by-one bug. writer.setMaxBufferedDocs(2) should work, but I had to stop the unit test because it's too slow because of the many disk accesses. Other things to try:\n\n-get stack trace of OOM (requires java 1.5)\n-use writer.setUseCompoundFile(false) and look at the index directory after the crash\n-use writer.setInfoStream(System.out) to get some (not much) more output from Lucene\n\nBTW, this seems to affect all big stored fields, not just binary fields.\n\n(Please reply here in the issue tracker, not on the mailing list. This way things can be properly tracked).\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=lucenebugs%40danielnaber.de",
            "name": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "key": "lucenebugs@danielnaber.de",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Daniel Naber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-01-22T22:35:23.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-01-22T22:35:23.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12327932/comment/12363628",
          "id": "12363628",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=georgew",
            "name": "georgew",
            "key": "georgew",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "george washington",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Daniel, a combination of :\n\n      iwriter.setMaxBufferedDocs(2);\n      iwriter.setMergeFactor(2);\n      iwriter.setUseCompoundFile(false);\n\nseems to help. I still get OOM errors but only with several larger docs (>10MB),  in succession, a significant improvement from the 5MB docs limit.\nPerhaps this issue should be kept open so that a more satisfactory solution is found.\nThank you for your help.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=georgew",
            "name": "georgew",
